codex
The probes confirm that `grep` treats dots in job names as wildcards, and that signal targets are used without rechecking their identity after the scan. Legacy records also remain unsafe when the recorded PID or group leader has actually been reused; the smoke tests only cover a missing old wrapper. The six-field format works with the requested readers, and the installed systemd documentation confirms that scopes inherit the caller’s environment.
